+## Design Notes
+
+**Canon flag (briefing rule 1 — flagged, not silently rewritten):** the 08-21 ruling's acceptance ("no lone-node scatter", cap ~5, new areas) supersedes the 08-17 "estates, but NOT 100% of the time" mix at the DEFAULT (attach 1000‰). The 08-17 doctrine is not deleted: `bias_prob_permille < 1000` restores the minority-isolate mix as a data option. The spatial-lane canon (2026-08-12, commits 2e3acab/8ece056) governs PIPE lane rendering — node placement does not touch it; no tension. Both flags land in the decision-log entry + PR body.
+
+**Why strict over emergent:** the emergent shape (b) is the current 5.12 mechanism — probabilistic strays can't satisfy "no lone nodes far from any cluster" deterministically. Strict (a) satisfies both acceptance maps by construction, matches "after ~5 nodes, go to a new area" literally, and reuses the existing attach machinery — the delta is two predicates + defaults. Draw counts per attempt are unchanged (the strict predicates are rejection predicates, like E31), so the rng interleaving shifts only through the acceptance outcome — re-bless is the deliberate, cause-documented 08-21 fold.
+
+**Implementation-time closures (beyond the spec's one-predicate delta — forced by the acceptance's "no third class, no strays", cause-documented in code + decision-log + PR body):** (1) `growth_attach_radius_ok` — the attach candidate must sit within the EUCLIDEAN radius of its anchor member; the 5.12 compass draw's diagonal directions placed candidates at up to dist×√2 (5.7–7.1 tiles) — outside radius, inside the seed floor: the exact third class (measured pre-fix: 7/19 = 37% of growth.dem spawns were strays under the strict lens). (2) The attach anchor is a LIVE TERMINAL only — the derived view leaves dead slots' id at 0, colliding with cluster 0's id (the fixture residential at slot 0), so a raw id match could anchor an attach on a ROUTER (a pre-existing 5.12 defect invisible to the old pins). Both are zero-draw rejection predicates; the anchor guard changes the eligible member set (no rng draws). KEEP both — the strict audit tests (`test_groups_estates_strict`, `test_groups_strict_audit_with_fixture`) pin them.
+
+**Seed distance default 10:** 2× the adjacency radius — visually distinct sections on the 40×30-tile map while staying within the era-3 connect span (18) for E31. The rejection budget keeps it honest on dense maps (deterministic skip, no stall).
